  "statement": "The Count-and-Say sequence is defined recursively:\n- countAndSay(1) = \"1\"\n- countAndSay(n) is the run-length encoding of countAndSay(n - 1) grouping contiguous identical digits. For example, \"3322251\" is read as \"two 3s, three 2s, one 5, one 1\" -> \"23321511\".\n\nGiven an integer N, generate and print countAndSay(N).",
  "inputFormat": "A single integer N.",
  "outputFormat": "Print the N-th term of the sequence as a string.",
  "constraints": "1 <= N <= 30",
  "sampleCases": [
    {
      "input": "1",
      "expectedOutput": "1",
      "explanation": "Base case."
    },
    {
      "input": "4",
      "expectedOutput": "1211",
      "explanation": "1 -> \"11\" -> \"21\" -> \"1211\"."
    }
  ],
